[1m[36mnix-search[0m - search nixpkgs packages and NixOS/Home Manager/darwin
options via search.nixos.org.

[1mUsage:[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m [33m[flags][0m [33m<query>[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m [33m<subcommand>[0m [33m[flags][0m [33m<query>[0m

[1mSubcommands:[0m
  [1m[36mpkgs[0m          nixpkgs packages (used when no subcommand is given)
  [1m[36mnixos[0m         NixOS module options, e.g. services.nginx.enable
  [1m[36mhome-manager[0m  Home Manager options, e.g. programs.git.enable
  [1m[36mdarwin[0m        nix-darwin options, e.g. system.defaults.dock.autohide
  [1m[36mservice[0m       options from service modules embedded in packages

[1mpkgs flags:[0m
  [1m[36m--name[0m      match attribute/package names only
  [1m[36m--programs[0m  match provided program/executable names

[1mGlobal flags:[0m
  [1m[36m-c, --channel[0m [33mCHANNEL[0m  nixpkgs channel: unstable, 26.05, ... (default: unstable)
  [1m[36m-s, --sort[0m [33mMODE[0m        sort results: relevance, alpha (default: relevance)
  [1m[36m-n, --max-results[0m [33mN[0m    maximum number of results (default: 50)
  [1m[36m-o, --output[0m [33mFORMAT[0m    output style: short, regular, long, json (default: regular)
  [1m[36m    --color[0m [33mMODE[0m       colorize output: auto, always, never (default: auto)
  [1m[36m-h, --help[0m             show this help
  [1m[36m    --version[0m          show the version

Global flags may appear before or after the subcommand, and values may be
attached (-n20) or separate (-n 20).

[1mExamples:[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m git                         [2m# packages (pkgs is the default)[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m pkgs --name firefox         [2m# match package names[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m pkgs --programs gcc         [2m# find packages shipping 'gcc'[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m nixos 'nginx enable'        [2m# NixOS options[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m home-manager programs.git   [2m# Home Manager options[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m -c 26.05 -s alpha -n 20 jq  [2m# channel 26.05, sorted by name[0m
  [1m[36mnix-search[0m -o json ffmpeg | jq         [2m# machine-readable output[0m
